# Windows batch files must have CRLF line endings.
#
# These were authored on macOS and committed with Unix (LF) endings. cmd.exe
# tolerates that for simple scripts, but mis-parses caret (^) line continuations
# and parenthesised blocks, which made install-windows.bat die on launch before
# it reached any pause — the window just flashed and closed with no error.
# Forcing CRLF here means the checkout is always correct on Windows regardless of
# which machine wrote the file.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repository.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
